  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "A random variable $X$ has the probability distribution given below.\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.05$ | $0.4$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$",
  "worked_solution": "If $X$ is a discrete random variable with probability mass function $f(x)$ and sample space $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each squared value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\sum }_{x\\in S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x) \\\\  & ={0}^{2}\\cdot 0.05+{1}^{2}\\cdot 0.4+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0.1+{3}^{2}\\cdot 0.25+{4}^{2}\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =0\\cdot 0.05+1\\cdot 0.4+4\\cdot 0.1+9\\cdot 0.25+16\\cdot 0.2 \\\\  & =6.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
